  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Extraction App**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the extraction app\'s structure. I want a polished React application that flawlessly implements the core features outlined in the design document. I\'m carefully reviewing the app\'s stages to ensure a solid foundation.\n\n\n**Refining the Session Flow**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the session flow. I\'ve broken it down into Topic Intake, Intention Setting, and Mode Selection. I am building a selection interface for the user to override AI mode recommendations. Finally, I\'m defining dynamic and engaging extraction modes with local persistence, including a \"Free Stream\" mode, and a \"Quick Fire\" mode that uses prompts generated by Gemini based on the topic.\n\n\n**Exploring Extraction Modes**\n\nI\'m expanding the extraction modes. I\'ve been thinking about several new interactive techniques to get the user\'s thoughts. Specifically, I\'m imagining interactive \"Guided Drill\" interviews, binary frame questions, \"Swipe/React\" interfaces for statement cards, sliders for intensity mapping, card sort clustering, and Timeline-based thought organization, all with Gemini integration to make them dynamically powerful!\n\n\n**Expanding Extraction Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into interactive methods to unlock thoughts. I\'m focusing on \"Finish the Sentence\" prompts, \"Devil\'s Advocate\" challenges, structured letter writing, and prioritizing actions. The \"Priority Pile\" concept is getting attention. I\'m excited by the possibilities! I\'m also planning the output, including markdown summaries, action items, and session history persistence.\n\nI\'ve also received feedback to remove multi-lingual support for now and simplify to a generic English app for organizing ideas into outlines or lists, which will focus our attention here and now.\n\n\n**Structuring the Application Code**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the application\'s code structure, and, per React guidelines, I\'m starting with well-defined TypeScript types to avoid token truncation issues. I\'m organizing the code into modular files: `types.ts` for shared interfaces; and client-side (or server-side) API calls for fetching from a Gemini API proxy. The server will handle topic induction.\n\n\n**Defining Mode Implementations**\n\nI\'m now implementing the AI-powered extraction modes. I\'m focusing on \"Quick Fire\" with `@google/genai`, \"Guided Drill\" question generation, \"Binary Framing\" for opposing interpretations, and \"Devil\'s Advocate\" challenges. The new synthesizer will create structured outputs. The app\'s structure includes `/components/` for Intake, Workspace, ModeSelector, and modes like FreeStream, QuickFire, GuidedDrill, BinaryFrame, and SwipeReact.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/types.ts` containing all the TypeScript interfaces, types, and enumerations needed for the dynamic Extraction session, including thoughts, modes, and steps."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 960981087
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
