  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Applying Bento Design**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refactoring `IntakeForm.tsx` to align with the bento design principles. Specifically, I\'m working to replace existing class and layout styles within the 175-536 line range. The plan is to proceed carefully, likely using `edit_file` to ensure a smooth transition.\n\n\n**Refining Layout and Style**\n\nI\'ve been working to replace those initial background and layout styles, and I\'ve updated the outer body and template pattern. I\'ve switched from `className=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 md:py-12\"` to `className=\"min-h-screen bento-pattern bg-[#F8F7F4] py-8 md:py-12 px-4 select-none\"`. I also realized the need to wrap inner card structures with a `max-w-5xl mx-auto space-y-6` container to preserve responsive centering. The header is being transformed into a stylish Title Bento card.\n\n\n**Transforming UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focused on refactoring the header section of the form. I\'m moving away from a simple paragraph and diving deep into a \"premium Bento-header card block.\" I have replaced the basic styles with a more visually engaging design including a black border with a shadow, a system version, a brain icon, and a prominent title. I am very proud of the new header!\n\n\n**Implementing New Font Pairings**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the new font pairing! The use of Space Grotesk and a serif, especially italic text-zinc-700, adds a beautiful touch to the Bento grid design. Now, I\'m focusing on the main layout division, transitioning from the old grid structure to a more modern one. I am also working on changes to borders and text styles inside the main block.\n\n\n**Styling Section Headings**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new session section styling. I\'ve designed a clean header with a numbered badge, using a black background and white text, and a strong font. The presets are styled in a grid with an outlined border, black border, and subtle hover effects for interactivity.\n\n\n**Refactoring UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating new components into the form, starting with the topic selection area. I\'m focusing on the button styling within the topic grid, and then I\'ll move on to the `textarea` element for input. I\'m refining the styles for the input field to match the rest of the Bento design. I am going for a cohesive look and feel. I\'m also planning to style the text area\'s labels.\n\n\n**Styling Component Options**\n\nI\'m now styling the option selection section. I\'m focusing on the component\'s font, display, and layout, and adding a numbered badge with a black background and white text, similar to the section heading style. I\'m making sure it matches my new bento-style design with a clean aesthetic and feel. I\'m adding a touch of interactivity through hover effects.\n\n\n**Adjusting Custom Input Field**\n\nI\'m now implementing the custom input field for the intention selection, using `AnimatePresence` for smooth transitions. I am focusing on making the input field styling consistent with the Bento design, ensuring it integrates seamlessly. The radio button styling is crucial, too. I\'m excited to refine the custom input.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will modify the first half of `src/components/IntakeForm.tsx` to apply the black-bordered, off-white bento card pattern with Space Grotesk and serif italic typography."
