  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Formulating Architectural Explanation**\n\nI\'ve got good news! The compilation went smoothly, which is a great start. My focus is now on crafting a clear architectural explanation that is highly focused on conversational aspects, and I aim to detail how the system switches to and uses it to drive the core.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The conversational interface was designed specifically to help you unburden your thoughts, push past cognitive roadblocks, and structure loose scattered ideas through interactive dialogue. \n\nHere is how the conversational flow works and how you can access it in the application:\n\n### 1. The Solitary Entry vs. Conversational Shift\n- **By Default // Free Stream Mode**: When you first state a topic and intention and launch a session, you are dropped into the basic **Free Stream** workspace. This is a solitary, quiet environment designed solely for quickly typing and dumping individual, top-down raw thoughts without any guidance.\n- **The Conversational Modules**: To interact conversationally with the AI, you can switch modules at any time using the horizontal **Jump Mode** tape at the top of your active workspace.\n\n### 2. Conversational Dialogue Centers\nClicking on the horizontal toolbar allows you to enter these specific dialog modes:\n- **`Guided Drill` (Interactive Interview)**: Gemini acts as a cognitive diagnostic guide. It reads your initial topic, your intention, and whatever thoughts you have already piled up, and dynamically formulates highly curated, deep follow-up questions to probe deeper. Your replies are captured and streamed directly into your surfaced pile.\n- **`Devil\'s Advocate` (Pressure Testing)**: Gemini analyzes your ideas and presents you with tough, provocative counterarguments, forcing you to defend your assumptions. Replying to these prompts creates structured, battle-tested concept nodes.\n\n### 3. How the Dialogue Feeds the Final Output\n1. Each response you type in **Guided Drill** or **Devil\'s Advocate** is instantly formatted and saved as a secure thought node.\n2. These nodes accumulate on the right-hand sidebar (**Surfaced Pile**).\n3. Once you have conversed enough to gather **5+ thoughts**, you click the **`Finish & Organize Outline`** button.\n4. Gemini aggregates every conversational turn, runs them through your advanced synthesis rules (e.g., standard prompting tone vs. socratic tone, cognitive bias diagnostics), and compiles a master structured **Markdown Blueprint and Action List**."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 113600087
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
