    thinking: "**Analyzing Implementation Approaches**\n\nI\'m currently focused on integrating the bi-directional conversational mode and speech-to-text functionalities into `GuidedDrill.tsx`. I\'m starting by exploring the structure of the bi-directional conversational mode, considering how a toggle could be incorporated within the `GuidedDrill.tsx` component.\n\n\n**Refining Conversational Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user interface for the conversational feature. A checkbox/toggle beneath the input will trigger a conversational mode. When activated, the placeholder text updates, and the API request changes to `/api/session/drill-clarify`. The API response will render directly in the timeline, with the updated question seamlessly following the response. The `QAHistory` structure is being re-evaluated to track conversational turns vs. question-answer turns, probably with an updated history format.\n\n\n**Defining Dialogue Implementation**\n\nI\'ve clarified the implementation steps for conversational flow. When `isDialogue` is active, the user\'s input goes to `/api/session/drill-clarify`, generating a response including `reply` and `nextQuestion`. The `qaHistory` will include `clarifyingReply` and `isDialogue`, and `currentQuestion` will be updated. The thought is being saved as `Clarification Request: \"User Input\" -> AI Response: \"Reply\"`.\n\n\n**Implementing Voice Dictation**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on adding voice dictation to the app, examining the standard Web Speech API. I\'m importing `Mic` and `MicOff` from `lucide-react` for the UI. I will implement a toggle that triggers `recognition.start()` when clicked, updating `isRecording`. The transcribed text will append to `answerDraft`. I\'m also preparing a bulletproof implementation, starting with a review of the `SpeechRecognition` setup.\n\n\n**Establishing Speech Recognition**\n\nI\'ve set up the `SpeechRecognition` object, checking for browser compatibility and initializing its properties. 