  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Component Visuals**\n\nI\'m currently focused on visually refining several components. Specifically, I\'m working on the modifications to the step badges for steps one, two, and three, and the custom selection colors in IntakeForm.tsx, lines 235-238. I think these tweaks will really improve the user experience.\n\n\n**Updating Badge Designs**\n\nI\'ve just updated the visual styling for the session step badges. I\'ve altered the styles to improve their clarity and visual hierarchy. Specifically, I\'ve replaced the black background and white text for the first step badge with a new color and border. I\'ve also kept the changes consistent with all current styles.\n\n\n**Adjusting Heading Styles**\n\nI\'m now revising the visual styling of section headings. I\'m focusing on the \"What do you want to get out of this?\" and \"Advanced Synthesis Controls\" sections. I plan to use the same badge style and shadow effect from step one, but with a new color, for a more consistent feel throughout the process. I am also working on standardizing the font styles.\n\n\n**Revising Color Palettes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on color choices. I want to make the selected options in the \"Intention\" step more visually engaging, moving away from solid black. I am aiming for more vibrant color selections to match the user\'s focus during this step, as well as keeping a consistent look for the visuals across different sections.\n\n\n**Enhancing Option Highlighting**\n\nI\'m currently revising the visual presentation of selected options. I\'m aiming for a more appealing and engaging selection highlight. Specifically, I\'m modifying the background of the selected option to have a rich yellow-amber color pop. I believe this change will significantly improve the visual feedback for users.\n\n\n"
